her callback)\n- dhcp6_ctl_readcommand @ 0x4182b8\n- dhcp6_ctl_acceptcommand @ 0x418504\n- sub_424080, sub_402660\n- get_duid @ 0x40f1d0\n\nThat's a lot. Focus: the AI review said \"main 经 get_duid 将 argv/网络数据传入 sub_40F0F8\". But get_duid takes 3 args (a1, a2, a3) and doesn't obviously call sub_40F0F8. Let me check get_duid @ 0x40f1d0 — maybe get_duid has a printf? Actually the bt for dhcp6s get_duid lists \"sub_40F168\" and \"sub_40CE98\" and dprintf. Hmm, sub_40F168 might be close to sub_40F0F8. Let me check.\n\nLet me get get_duid source and search for callers of sys_run_command (maybe named sub_40F0F8 in call graph). Also fetch sub_404BE0 brief and dhcp6_ctl_readcommand brief.","stream":true,"block":0}

