data: {"seq":216,"ts":"2026-08-22T19:17:13.572Z","text":"08b08601 = xl2tpd! It was EXCLUDED in identification as \"not-public\" (l2tp: infrastructure/control daemon). But xl2tpd listens on UDP 1701 and handles L2TP control packets from the internet — many routers have xl2tpd exposed. The identification gate says xl2tpd excluded as infrastructure. But the attack surface graph still has high-scored paths for it. The user explicitly said \"httpd/minidlna/dhcp6","stream":true,"block":0}

event: thinking
data: {"seq":217,"ts":"2026-08-22T19:17:13.952Z","text":"08b08601 = xl2tpd! It was EXCLUDED in identification as \"not-public\" (l2tp: infrastructure/control daemon). But xl2tpd listens on UDP 1701 and handles L2TP control packets from the internet — many routers have xl2tpd exposed. The identification gate says xl2tpd excluded as infrastructure. But the attack surface graph still has high-scored paths for it. The user explicitly said \"httpd/minidlna/dhcp6s 等\" — xl2tpd not in the list, plus it's excluded. But it's a P0 bof (network_thread strcpy) and P1 cmdi (start_pppd). L2TP control packets on UDP 1701 can carry attacker-chosen tunnel attributes (hostname, etc.) that feed start_pppd → pppd command line! That's a classic xl2tpd CVE","stream":true,"block":0}

