es support threads via clone). The connection reset could be because httpd's accept loop runs in a thread that qemu can't schedule properly, or the select loop rejected the connection because the request wasn't a valid \"GET /... HTTP/1.1\" with Host? The harness sends proper GET though.\n\nLet me look at whether there are prior failed traces with httpd \"ConnectionResetError\" — that means TCP connect succeeded and peer closed. So httpd IS listening and accepting. Good sign. Maybe it needs a specific path that exists in /web. The request \"/\" triggered reset too. Hmm, if httpd requires Authorization header in response to 401... it would send 401 then close. \"Connection reset\" though means RST, not normal close. Maybe the process crashed on the connection (RST when process closes abruptly). Interesting — could itself be a crash. But \"empty diff\" and 30-55 baseline functions.\n\nTo make httpd traces meaningful, we should compare two different requests (baseline vs trigger) — the tool does baseline run vs trigger run. The trigger error means zero diff; the trigger didn't reach the handler. Need httpd to actually respond. Options:\n1. Provide argv that makes httpd run in foreground with a spec. e.g. httpd -p 80? or -f? TP-Link httpd usage: httpd [-p port] [-c config]. Let me check httpd main.\n\nLet me read httpd main (0x...). httpd md5 9582aa23. Search \"main\" → get the address. Actually from the earlier brief, binary httpd has 4882 functions. main address? Let me search.\n\nAlso for minidlna: trace with argv -d -i lo got 47 funcs, refused connection. minidlna default: reads /etc/minidlna.conf, binds 8200. With -d (debug, no daemon) and -i lo... maybe it needs `-f` (foreground). Actually -d is \"daemonize\"? In minidlna: -d = debug (no daemon, log to stderr)? Options: -f foreground, -d debug... Let me check minidlna man: -d = debug, stays in foreground? minidlna options: -f (foreground), -d (debug output)... The trace harness may kill before binding. 47 functions baseline means it ran some code. Connection refused at 8200 means","stream":true,"block":0}

