data: {"seq":409,"ts":"2026-08-22T19:18:28.709Z","text":"httpBase64decode: bounded writes (checks v6+2-v20 < v4), decent. But note: writes `*(a2+v6)=0` at end via v17=v6 — if a3 (outlen) small, the terminating NUL at a2+v6 may be out of bounds? v6 could reach v4 (out length limit was only applied to the inner 3-byte writes; the terminating `*(a2+v6)=0` has no bound check!). If v6 == v4 (exactly filled output), writing terminator at a2[v4] is one byte overlap of caller buffer — likely within the caller's struct (usually +1 spare). Not strong.\n\nOK. Let me now do dynamic runs. Action plan (parallel where possible; note only one trace at a time — 409 risk):\n\n1. First: fw_request_trace httpd port 80 /userRpm/PingIframeRpm.htm (test handler reachability).\nWhile that runs, I can't start another trace (409). But I CAN request fuzz runs (different subsystem - fuzz budget). Let me kick off:\n- fuzz: minidlna ParseNameValue (0x41c8f8) args [str,len,out,base] — hypothesis: \"name:value\" parse into fixed result buffer; malformed input may overflow.\nActually wait, look at ParseNameValue: v5[0]=a1 (name ptr), v5[3]=a2 (len?), then parsexml(a3 struct?) — parsexml sets a1[2]=*a1; a1[1]=*a1+a1[3] — it treats a1 as a parse-context struct with buffer ptr/len. ParseNameValue(a1=name, a2=len, a3=&result, a4=base?). The 4th arg a4 is base address. Hmm signature (int a1, int a2, _DWORD *a3, int a4) — this is the classic minidlna ParseNameValue(buf, len, &name, &value)? In stock minidlna: ParseNameValue(const char *text, int textlen, char **name, char **value) — splits \"k=v\" or \"k: v\". It calls parsexml? no, stock uses ixml... this version differs.\n\nFuzz arg spec only supports [buf,len] type specs. Let me pass args [\"buf\",\"len\",\"u32\",\"u32\"]? The doc says arg spec e.g. [buf,len]. I'll try [\"buf\",\"len\"].\n\nActually for a cleaner hypothesis, let me reconsider minidlna main HTTP loop. The core packet handling: Process_upnphttp reads request into buffer, then GetHTTPResponse dispatch: sub_40D1FC etc. The memmove(dest, src, *(a1+112)) in sub_40D1FC: a1+112 might be content-length. sub_40D1FC is the GET dispatcher.\n\nLet me look at minidlna's actual recv + dispatch: Process_upnphttp @ ... let me search. Actually in surface: \"Process_upnphttp\" — find its address via search.\n\nI'm spending a lot of tool calls. Let me be decisive:\n\nDynamic batch now:\n1. fw_request_trace httpd 9582aa23 port 80 \"/userRpm/PingIframeRpm.htm?doType=ping&ping_addr=127.0.0.1&isNew=new\" — request_path with query? The tool says request_path — likely just path. Use \"/userRpm/PingIframeRpm.htm\".\n2. fw_request_fuzz minidlna 3e3258c9 function 0x41c8f8 args [buf,len] seconds 120.\n\nThen poll.","stream":true,"block":0}

