data: {"seq":428,"ts":"2026-08-22T19:18:35.459Z","text":"Both still running. Let me use the time to check uclited's network listener and the minidlna sys_run_command (0x405594 etc.), plus look at dhcp6s control channel port. Actually let me focus on getting a real finding. Candidates so far:\n\n1. httpd: need to find a command injection. The best-known TP-Link C7v2 httpd vulns: \"system() in... \"? Actually old C7 uses different httpd. This firmware 3.15.4 has the newer httpd+uclited. Known CVEs for this family: CVE-2017-13772 (TP-Link WR940N ping cmd injection), CVE-2020-XXXX... The ping handler here uses raw sockets (fixed). \n\nLet me look at other httpd handlers that run shell: search for system in httpd with string args. In httpd, common: \"swShutdown\", \"Tracert\"... Try searching \"system\" won't work. Let me search function names with \"System\" or \"save\" handlers...\n\nAlternative high-probability: uclited is on TCP (IN-011) — check its listen port. uclited is the switch to operate without httpd auth? On TP-Link, uclited listens on 0.0.0.0:6666 or","stream":true,"block":0}

event: thinking
data: {"seq":429,"ts":"2026-08-22T19:18:35.854Z","text":"Both still running. Let me use the time to check uclited's network listener and the minidlna sys_run_command (0x405594 etc.), plus look at dhcp6s control channel port. Actually let me focus on getting a real finding. Candidates so far:\n\n1. httpd: need to find a command injection. The best-known TP-Link C7v2 httpd vulns: \"system() in... \"? Actually old C7 uses different httpd. This firmware 3.15.4 has the newer httpd+uclited. Known CVEs for this family: CVE-2017-13772 (TP-Link WR940N ping cmd injection), CVE-2020-XXXX... The ping handler here uses raw sockets (fixed). \n\nLet me look at other httpd handlers that run shell: search for system in httpd with string args. In httpd, common: \"swShutdown\", \"Tracert\"... Try searching \"system\" won't work. Let me search function names with \"System\" or \"save\" handlers...\n\nAlternative high-probability: uclited is on TCP (IN-011) — check its listen port. uclited is the switch to operate without httpd auth? On TP-Link, uclited listens on 0.0.0.0:6666 or unix /var/uclited? Actually the newer TP-Link uses \"ipc\" over TCP port 6666 without auth?? Not sure.\n\nLet me read uclited main 0x5009f0 brief.","stream":true,"block":0}

