data: {"seq":474,"ts":"2026-08-22T19:18:58.266Z","text":"Trace: httpd with -I -p 80 → connection refused, baseline 9 functions (only startup, no listen). httpd did not bind with -I? The -I flag might mean \"validate init\". Let me check httpd usage. Actually with no argv before it also refused (reset). Hmm previous trace with argv[] got \"ConnectionReset\" — that means it DID accept. But this run with -I -p 80 refused. So -I is wrong.\n\nFuzz: handshake failed for minidlna ParseNameValue — \"目标函数在正常启动流程中未被到达\". Per instructions: 改整二进制 (只传 binary_md5). minidlna whole-binary fuzz with argv: minidlnad in qemu needs config... Let me try whole-binary mode: fw_request_fuzz binary_md5 only (function omitted) — that runs the whole program with AFL argv/stdin? For a daemon that needs config, might fail too. Let me try with seconds 120 (whole binary).\n\nAlso httpd trace: use argv [] again (worked to get connection reset = accepted). Actually connection reset means accept but close; still no diff. The httpd process under qemu may not process because it forks worker","stream":true,"block":0}

