rom stdin? minidlnad doesn't read stdin. It's a daemon; the persistent hook needs the target function to be naturally reached during startup. Parsers aren't reached at startup.\n\nBetter: fuzz dhcp6s? Whole binary dhcp6c/dhcp6s also not natural.\n\nPractical approach: pick functions reachable during minidlnad startup? e.g., ParseNameValue? Not reached at startup. Hmm.\n\nLet me reconsider httpd: there might be a NATIVE qemu run where httpd actually listens: In the previous traces (argv=[], port 80), the request triggered \"ConnectionResetError\" — connection accepted then closed. The baseline split showed 30-55 functions. It may be that httpd DID handle the request: TP-Link httpd on invalid/no auth sends \"401 Unauthorized\\nConnection: close\" then closes. RST could result from unread data / SO_LINGER. diff=0 means trigger functions == baseline functions exactly (both runs identical coverage). Old traces showed 30 vs","stream":true,"block":0}

