data: {"seq":513,"ts":"2026-08-22T19:19:17.682Z","text":"httpd is started with no args: \"/usr/bin/httpd &\". So argv should be empty (previous traces did that and got accept+reset — meaning it IS listening). The connection reset is likely httpd responding 401 + closing. But diff empty. Perhaps the harness's GET lacks a Host header or proper method? The trigger_result for \"/\" and \"/userRpm/LoginRpm.htm\" both show connection reset (bytes 0). httpd sends \"HTTP/1.1 401 Unauthorized\" then RST? bytes 0 though.\n\nActually maybe httpd needs to have its shared memory / config from uboot env, and without it, the worker thread that handles requests is never created. httpd main: selected worker threads... If requests hang, harness times out then closes → RST. But diff==0 means no extra functions executed, so request never reached the handler.\n\nqemu-user: multi-threading via clone works. But httpd might use sigwait or mq... The 9-func run with -I shows; with","stream":true,"block":0}

