data: {"seq":522,"ts":"2026-08-22T19:19:20.854Z","text":"httpd is started with no args: \"/usr/bin/httpd &\". So argv should be empty (previous traces did that and got accept+reset — meaning it IS listening). The connection reset is likely httpd responding 401 + closing. But diff empty. Perhaps the harness's GET lacks a Host header or proper method? The trigger_result for \"/\" and \"/userRpm/LoginRpm.htm\" both show connection reset (bytes 0). httpd sends \"HTTP/1.1 401 Unauthorized\" then RST? bytes 0 though.\n\nActually maybe httpd needs to have its shared memory / config from uboot env, and without it, the worker thread that handles requests is never created. httpd main: selected worker threads... If requests hang, harness times out then closes → RST. But diff==0 means no extra functions executed, so request never reached the handler.\n\nqemu-user: multi-threading via clone works. But httpd might use sigwait or mq... The 9-func run with -I shows; with no args 30-55 funcs. Let me try the trace again with argv [] and request \"/userRpm/LoginRpm.htm\" to reconfirm while I do fuzz whole-binary httpd? Whole-binary fuzz of httpd needs stdin/args — can't naturally feed HTTP.\n\nBetter idea: fuzz targets that ARE start-reachable:\n- dhcp6c/dhcp6s: main parses config file via cfparse (yyparse) — not network.\n- minidlnad: at startup it does readoptionsfile → ParseNameValue? no.\n\nGiven function-level fuzz on minidlnad start-reachable functions... Actually maybe easier: try whole-binary fuzz for minidlnad with argv [\"-f\",\"-d\"] and see if AFC can run it reading from stdin (it won't, it'll block on sockets; forkserver handshake may succeed though since process starts). Whole-binary mode: AFL feeds stdin as fuzz input; minidlnad ignores stdin, so no progress. Bad.\n\nLet me reconsider: which network-parser functions are naturally reached at process start? For httpd: none (main loop waits for connections).\n\nAlternative dynamic approach: frida (x86 only) — no.\n\nOK — maybe the trace mechanism CAN reach httpd if given the right trigger. Let me check how trace triggers: \"kind= http_get\". It connects to 127.0.0.1:port and sends \"GET path HTTP/1.1\". For httpd this failed with reset for LoginRpm.htm. But wait — trace c6bb8ac732fb minidlna with -d -i lo: refused. b13c28e670b7 httpd argv[]: reset. All requests ended in error → the harness marks trigger_error and diff empty.\n\nHmm, what if httpd actually needs UDP 53/dns or /tmp files: httpd on boot reads /etc/dhcp6sctlkey etc. Or maybe it requires the \"ubootenv\" variable. Without lan interface configured, the http server still binds.\n\nLet me try one more time with argv [] and see if it listens this time (maybe requires retries; the last empty-argv attempts were 16:48-16:55, all reset). I'll re-run with argv [] but different path \"/userRpm/StatusRpm.htm\". Also run the minidlna whole-binary-ish trace again with proper config: minidlna needs /etc/minidlna.conf? Let me check what minidlnad reads: readoptionsfile reads /etc/minidlna.conf by default. The firmware likely lacks it → minidlna exits immediately? But baseline showed 40-47 functions. Let me check the firmware for minidlna.conf.","stream":false,"block":0}

