cpAccept. Let me read wmnetTcpAccept/sub_4459C0 and how the request gets read (wmnetTcpRead) and dispatched. If the accept is in the MAIN thread (select loop), then under qemu it should work. The \"Connection reset\" could be because the harness sent HTTP/1.1 GET without \"Connection: close\" and httpd waits for more, then harness closes → httpd sends RST? bytes=0 though.\n\nActually, maybe the trigger request needs to hit a port httpd actually binds IN the sandbox network namespace. qemu-user runs as the sandbox process; binding 0.0.0.0:80 inside a docker container conflicts with nothing. 127.0.0.1:80 in the container → the harness connects to container localhost:80. Should work.\n\nLet me try again with argv [] — real quick run — but the previous 4 attempts all reset","stream":true,"block":0}

