work. What about dhcp6_ctl paths? dhcp6s control channel (if enabled): dhcp6_ctl_init(off_43C070 keyfile, off_43C074 ctlport, 5, &dword_43C060). If `dword_43C608` is true — set when keyfile provided (-k /etc/dhcp6sctlkey is in firmware!). ctlport default: from main, off_43C074 default NULL → passed \"\" → dhcp6_ctl_init with default port 5470? Actually for dhcp6s the ctl socket binds to UDP 5470 on loopback? or TCP? In kame dhcp6, dhcp6_ctl_init uses unix domain socket! Yes — dhcp6ctl uses UNIX domain socket /var/run/dhcp6s.sock (or similar), NOT TCP. So not network-exposed. Good — dynamic trace failed anyway (no TCP listener).\n\nSo for dhcp6s, the honest result: no network-reachable sink found in the high-scored path (debug-echo only, argv-driven). But WAIT — sub_4065B4's own code: `v98[8]` etc... and the relay handling with `dhcp6_vbuf_copy(v25+13, v117)`... v25 = malloc(0x3C); v25+13 is offset 52; dhcp6_vbuf_copy(v25+13, v117) copies at +52 (8 bytes = 52..59), v25[11] = +44 (8 bytes 44..51), v25[14] = +56 (v34 = v25[14]; dst for inner packet). So v25[13] (offset 52) copies optinfo (2 words), v25[11] (offset 44) → 2 words... those are within the 0x3C (60) struct: offsets 44-51 and 52-59, both 8-byte. ✓ safe.\n\nThe **relay-forward inner packet** loop: `v23 = v87[0]` (inner msg len); `v34 = (char *)v25[14]; v7 = &v34[v23]; v19 = v34;` — hmm it takes the inner packet from v87 optinfo (relay msg option) — v87 was filled by dhcp6_get_options on the outer message. That's heap growing — safe-ish.\n\nAlright. Given diminishing returns and the fuzz still running, let me now:\n1. Wait/poll fuzz once more.\n2. Record the execWlanCmd overflow as static-only (uclited is IN-011 TCP input!) — wait, is uclited network reachable? IN-011 uclited TCP — yes it IS in the inputs list (candidate grade). But is the TCP port real? uclited binds?? Later traces tried port 80 and got refused. Let me quickly check ucm_msgTaskCreate for socket creation to determine if uclited network-facing and on what port. If uclited is genuinely TCP-facing, then execWlanCmd overflow reachable? The overflow input (a3 = essid/key) comes from config ops (ucm protocol) — reachable if the ucm protocol is accessible over TCP without auth. Many Archer C7 newer builds: httpd and uclited communicate over TCP 6666 loopback only (or unix). IN-011 gate classified as TCP (candidate).\n\nTime to wrap: I'll do a final round: check ucm_msgTaskCreate + poll fuzz.","stream":true,"block":0}

