data: {"seq":876,"ts":"2026-08-22T19:21:57.321Z","text":"KEY: uclited's TCP listener:\n- socket/bind: binds 127.0.0.1:51237 (v3=*v1=51237; addr.sa_data[2]=2130706433=127.0.0.1) — LOOPBACK ONLY!\n- accept checks: `if ((sa_data[2] & 0xFF000000) != 0x7F000000) close()` — rejects non-127.0.0.1 connections explicitly.\n\nSo uclited TCP is loopback-only. NOT a public input (the identification gate over-flagged it). The execWlanCmd chain requires the web UI (authenticated admin) on httpd → loopback IPC → uclited. Not remote-exploitable without auth.\n\nOK this closes uclited too","stream":true,"block":0}

