data: {"seq":916,"ts":"2026-08-22T19:22:13.602Z","text":"setStatus is just printf + global state; setDns writes to globals (unk_441358/unk_441380) with printf — no system.\n\nSo dhcp6c's network-derived data only goes to printf/globals, not to shell. The debugInfo system() is with numeric status. No injection.\n\nFINAL POLL of the fuzz, then compose results. If fuzz still running/stuck, I'll report status and not invent crashes.\n\nActually, one more valuable thing to verify quickly — the minidlna `sub_405594` path is config-driven; but what about `SendResp_thumbnail(a1, v12)` where v12 is the 500-byte buffer INSIDE sub_40D1FC's frame, and URL bytes were copied into v8 (the 512-region) — SendResp_thumbnail may copy URL-param-derived object id into v12 with sprintf, potentially overflowing if the handler itself doesn't bound. But that again is within-sub_40D1FC decompile uncertainty.\n\nGiven diminishing time, let me finalize: poll fuzz one last time; then write the summary. I will NOT record low-confidence speculative findings, but I should record what's legitimately established. Among all candidates, the only *real* code-level defects with solid pseudo-C evidence:\n\n1. uclited execWlanCmd: case7/15/21 quote-wrapper writes into v21[132] with 3×len, and only case 7 checks len<33; cases 15/21 do NOT bound-check — stack overflow potential; a2/a3 come from uclited's config IPC, which is loopback-only + auth-gated (httpd admin). Severity low/medium; static-only; CWE-121. Chain: httpd(authenticated WlanRpm) → ucm cfg IPC(127.0.0.1:51237) → ucm_cfg_handler → swWlanSetConfig → execWlanCmd(0x49c84c) → v21 overflow. This is a legit finding but weak attacker value (needs admin).\n\n2. dhcp6c vsprintf wrapper sub_40D068 (sys_run_command_2) — same debug echo family; non-network.\n\nActually, hmm, wait — let me reconsider #1's reachability more carefully: is there any NON-auth path to ucm? The accept check restricts to 127.0.0.1 but httpd itself is the one sending. httpd handlers for WLAN settings require login (HttpAccessPermit). So requires admin credentials (default admin/admin on TP-Link — often unchanged!). Default creds admin/admin is a real precondition. Still \"static-only\" confidence.\n\nAlso for minidlna: nothing exploitable confirmed without config.\n\nGiven the user explicitly asked \"继续挖 httpd/minidlna/dhcp6s 等，必须自己调用 fw_request_trace/fw_get_trace 和 fw_request_fuzz/fw_get_fuzz_run\" — I've done that:\n- traces: httpd ×(several, incl. fresh 822e53e6595c), minidlna (previous), dhcp6s (70540a334abd)\n- fuzz: fz-6b17d0a9 (function,","stream":true,"block":0}

