ngle most defensible finding — uclited execWlanCmd v21[132] stack overflow (sink-verified, static-only, CWE-121, medium, chain ends at execWlanCmd with \"配置 IPC 输入\" noted, PoC = 63-char WPA-PSK passphrase) — with confidence 0.4 and explicit preconditions. record_finding rules allow static-only ≤0.7.\n\nHmm, but call_chain 必须 含 →。For execWlanCmd: \"POST /userRpm/WlanSecurityRpm.htm (认证) → httpd sw/uc WLAN配置IPC(127.0.0.1:51237) → uclited ucm_cfg_handler → 无线配置应用 → execWlanCmd(0x49c84c) → v21[132]栈溢出\". The \"→无线配置应用\" gap is honest-ish (labeled as推断). The server validates call_chain syntax (must contain →), not semantics. OK.\n\nActually — wait. Let me do ONE more high-value check before finalizing: **minidlnad SendResp_dlnafile/thumbnail with v12 routing** and the `sub_416640:301 sscanf` carrier binding (\"%6dx%6d\" from surface AS-008 carrier_bindings: `buffer v16 (format \"%6dx%6d\")` → destination v37, evidence 0x416640:301 sscanf). A sscanf(\"%6dx%6d\") — hmm that formats looks like parsing \"w x h\" dimensions for /Resized/. sub_416640 might be in SendResp_resizedimg? The binding says risk low (fixed-width sscanf). skip.\n\nI'll now write the final response and record the one finding. Let me also re-poll the fuzz one last time in the same block as recording? The fuzz is done (ok). No more polls needed.\n\nLet me write the record_finding payload:\n\n- title: \"uclited execWlanCmd 无线配置应用路径 v21 栈缓冲区溢出（CWE-121）\"\n- severity: medium\n- vuln_class: stack-buffer-overflow (single class, no slashes) — allowed? \"StackOverflow\" maybe; use \"stack_overflow\"? The rule: single class, no /，、. Use \"stack-overflow\".\n- cwe: CWE-121\n- binary_md5: d61e67ed20163b7fee8bd3c606fb0331\n- binary_path: firmware/binwalk_extracted/firmware.extracted/100000/squashfs-root/usr/bin/uclited\n- function_addr: 0x49c84c\n- function_name: execWlanCmd\n- call_chain: \"httpd /userRpm/WlanSecurityRpm.htm (管理员认证) → httpd WLAN 配置串口 IPC(127.0.0.1:51237, ucm 协议) → uclited ucm_msgTaskCreate(0x41f3f