m and treat \"RST\" as evidence per orchestrator.\n\nLet me start with searches: Ddns/DynDns in httpd; also \"NasShare\" / \"samba\" related execs; also \"iptables\" sprintf with user strings in httpd (search \"Ipv6Firewall\"? too broad).\n\nAlso — the orchestrator mentioned \"上一轮 dhcp6s 整二进制有 50746 execs\" — implying a dhcp6s whole-binary fuzz already ran successfully (someone ran it). I can request another whole-binary fuzz for dhcp6s (md5 23e37960) with seconds 120 and poll. Whole-binary dhcp6s with argv [\"eth0\"] will exercise main→cfparse... Actually whole-binary mode argv: the tool takes argv? fw_request_fuzz has no argv param in whole-binary mode... Looking at schema: args (arg spec) and function, plus binary_md5, seconds. No argv. In whole-binary","stream":true,"block":0}

