build iptables commands with port numbers (atoi → decimal, safe). ExecuteDmzCfg in httpd: uses IPs (validated).\n\n   - What about httpd \"url filter\" / \"mac filter\" iptables entries with strings? Look at functions in httpd that sprintf+system with HTTP-derived strings.\n\n3. Also the SMB (IN-015 samba_multicall port 445) — smbd is a big attack surface; smbpasswd IN-010. Samba on this firmware is old (Samba 3.x) - known CVEs? We can't easily mine samba (16MB binary? it's statically linked?). Actually samba_multicall contains smbd; 445 public. Dynamic: trace smbd? It's tiny? Let me check.\n\n4. uclited DHCP server DHCPCfg (ExecuteDhcpStaticRoute 0x4401ac) - iptables with IPs.\n\nLet me prioritize:\nA. httpd: find sprintf+system with HTTP-parameter-derived STRING (not numeric/IP). Typical TP-Link suspects: hostname (WAN hostname, DDNS), USB device name, share folder name... Search httpd for sprintf+system patterns involving httpGetEnv strings. Since I can't grep decompiled source globally, use attack-surface paths filtered... The surface graph returned only top-50 by score for all binaries; httpd didn't appear. I need a different entry: search httpd function names \"DynDns\" (DDNS updates often build curl/wget commands), \"HostName\", \"NetBIOS\", \"nas\".\n\nDDNS is a strong candidate: m_wiz... TP-Link DDNS: \"dyndns.org\" update executed via wget? in httpd \"wm_dns\"... let me search \"DynDns\" / \"Ddns\".\n\nB. NAS Samba: uclited \"nasSambaCfgFileWriteMainSec\" (0x4a546c) writes smb.conf; then samba restarted by? Also httpd \"swNasUpdateShareFolders\". And smbd itself on 445: huge attack surface, old Samba known bugs (CVE-2015-0240 etc). Fuzz smbd? smbd whole binary fuzz might work (it reads stdin? no).\n\nC. Dynamic: request fuzz for httpd whole binary (argv []?) — httpd may fail. Or vsftpd whole-binary (FTP port 21, IN-012): vsftpd reads config and runs; whole-binary fuzz feeds stdin — vsftpd ignores stdin. Hmm.\n\nD. Trace httpd again with argv [] to reconfirm and treat \"RST\" as evidence per orchestrator.\n\nLet me start with searches: Ddns/DynDns in httpd; also \"NasShare\" / \"samba\" related execs; also \"iptables\" sprintf with user strings in httpd (search \"Ipv6Firewall\"? too broad).\n\nAlso — the orchestrator mentioned \"上一轮 dhcp6s 整二进制有 50746 execs\" — implying a dhcp6s whole-binary fuzz already ran successfully (someone ran it). I can request another whole-binary fuzz for dhcp6s (md5 23e37960) with seconds 120 and poll. Whole-binary dhcp6s with argv [\"eth0\"] will exercise main→cfparse... Actually whole-binary mode argv: the tool takes argv? fw_request_fuzz has no argv param in whole-binary mode... Looking at schema: args (arg spec) and function, plus binary_md5, seconds. No argv. In whole-binary mode, the binary runs with no args → dhcp6s usage error → exits; but AFL may still count execs via stdin injection into... dhcp6s no stdin. But orchestrator says 50746 execs happened for dhcp6s — so whole-binary mode generates execs anyway","stream":true,"block":0}

