data: {"seq":1180,"ts":"2026-08-22T19:29:09.047Z","text":"The orchestrator says: don't stop. Continue mining high-score attack paths: httpd/NAS Samba/command injection etc, static+dynamic. record_finding must have call_chain and poc. Poll fuzz runs until ok/error. Use whole-binary fuzz when function-level handshake fails. Use existing qemu results (RST/refused) as evidence.\n\nPlan for this round:\n1. Re-poll the dhcp6s whole-binary fuzz mentioned (\"上一轮 dhcp6s 整二进制有 50746 execs\") — wait, that was dhcp6s whole binary? The orchestrator says \"上一轮 dhcp6s 整二进制有 50746 execs\" — meaning there was a fuzz run on dhcp6s whole binary with 50746 execs that I should check. Let me list fuzz runs? There's no fw_list_fuzzs tool... I only have fw_get_fuzz_run with run_id. I don't know the run_id of that dhcp6s run. Hmm. Maybe the orchestrator refers to something done between turns. I can't list runs. I could request a new whole-binary fuzz for dhcp6s myself.\n\n2. Attack surfaces to mine:\n   - httpd command injection (NAS Samba config file write → samba start command?)\n   - NAS Samba: samba_multicall / smbd; the NAS share config flows from httpd → /etc/samba/smb.conf write → restart samba. Path: swNasUpdateShareFolders etc. Look at httpd NAS functions that write smb.conf with user-controlled share names/paths, then run samba daemon. There's \"nasSambaCfgFileWriteMainSec\" in uclited. Let me examine uclited NAS samba config write → command exec (smbd restart). If share name from HTTP POST goes into smb.conf unescaped... smb.conf injection isn't command injection. But uclited might restart samba via system(\"smbd restart\")...\n\n   - Command injection in httpd: maybe in \"UpnpPortMapping\"? No, that's uclited igd functions writing iptables. Look for iptables sprintf+system in httpd with HTTP params (e.g., PortForwarding / Nat table handlers!). httpd \"igDAddPortMapping\" in uclited? Those functions: ExecuteVsTable, ExecutePtTable (virtual server / port trigger)! In uclited they build iptables commands with port numbers (atoi → decimal, safe). ExecuteDmzCfg in httpd: uses IPs (validated).\n\n   - What about httpd \"url filter\" / \"mac filter\" iptables entries with strings? Look at functions in httpd that sprintf+system with HTTP-derived strings.\n\n3. Also the SMB (IN-015 samba_multicall port 445) — smbd is a big attack surface; smbpasswd IN-010. Samba on this firmware is old (Samba 3.x) - known CVEs? We can't easily mine samba (16MB binary? it's statically linked?). Actually samba_multicall contains smbd; 445 public. Dynamic: trace smbd? It's tiny? Let me check.\n\n4. uclited DHCP server DHCPCfg (ExecuteDhcpStaticRoute 0x4401ac) - iptables with IPs.\n\nLet me prioritize:\nA. httpd: find sprintf+system with HTTP-parameter-derived STRING (not numeric/IP). Typical TP-Link suspects: hostname (WAN hostname, DDNS), USB device name, share folder name... Search httpd for sprintf+system patterns involving httpGetEnv strings. Since I can't grep decompiled source globally, use attack-surface paths filtered... The surface graph returned only top-50 by score for all binaries; httpd didn't appear. I need a different entry: search httpd function names \"DynDns\" (DDNS updates often build curl/wget commands), \"HostName\", \"NetBIOS\", \"nas\".\n\nDDNS is a strong candidate: m_wiz... TP-Link DDNS: \"dyndns.org\" update executed via wget? in httpd \"wm_dns\"... let me search \"DynDns\" / \"Ddns\".\n\nB. NAS Samba: uclited \"nasSambaCfgFileWriteMainSec\" (0x4a546c) writes smb.conf; then samba restarted by? Also httpd \"swNasUpdateShareFolders\". And smbd itself on 445: huge attack surface, old Samba known bugs (CVE-2015-0240 etc). Fuzz smbd? smbd whole binary fuzz might work (it reads stdin? no).\n\nC. Dynamic: request fuzz for httpd whole binary (argv []?) — httpd may fail. Or vsftpd whole-binary (FTP port 21, IN-012): vsftpd reads config and runs; whole-binary fuzz feeds stdin — vsftpd ignores stdin. Hmm.\n\nD. Trace httpd again with argv [] to reconfirm and treat \"RST\" as evidence per orchestrator.\n\nLet me start with searches: Ddns/DynDns in httpd; also \"NasShare\" / \"samba\" related execs; also \"iptables\" sprintf with user strings in httpd (search \"Ipv6Firewall\"? too broad).\n\nAlso — the orchestrator mentioned \"上一轮 dhcp6s 整二进制有 50746 execs\" — implying a dhcp6s whole-binary fuzz already ran successfully (someone ran it). I can request another whole-binary fuzz for dhcp6s (md5 23e37960) with seconds 120 and poll. Whole-binary dhcp6s with argv [\"eth0\"] will exercise main→cfparse... Actually whole-binary mode argv: the tool takes argv? fw_request_fuzz has no argv param in whole-binary mode... Looking at schema: args (arg spec) and function, plus binary_md5, seconds. No argv. In whole-binary mode, the binary runs with no args → dhcp6s usage error → exits; but AFL may still count execs via stdin injection into... dhcp6s no stdin. But orchestrator says 50746 execs happened for dhcp6s — so whole-binary mode generates execs anyway (it fuzzes argv/stdin through the qemu-afl bootstrap). OK, request whole-binary dhcp6s fuzz and poll.\n\nPlan of actions now:\n1. fw_request_fuzz dhcp6s whole binary (md5 23e37960, seconds 120) + fw_search Ddns/DynDns patterns. (parallel)\n\nThen continue static on httpd NAS/samba & ddns; poll fuzz; maybe fuzz httpd whole binary too.\n\nLet me also examine smb.conf writing path for command execution: uclited nasSambaCfgFileWriteMainSec → maybe uclited calls \"system(\"/etc/init.d/samba restart\")\"? Search samba exec paths in uclited: pattern \"Samba\".","stream":true,"block":0}

