it if username is s[1..16] (64 bytes 4..67), pwd s[17..31] (64 bytes 68..131), then s[32..101] = cliUrl? s[103] would be... Let me not over-analyze: copies are bounded 63/127 bytes; everything within s[]. Only overlaps. Not a vuln.\n\nThe interesting exec part: swDdnsStart(v2, 2) — starts DDNS updater. That's where command injection might be: DDNS start builds wget/curl command with the provider URL & credentials. swDdnsStart is in uclited? Or httpd? Let me find swDdnsStart and get_dyn_state, suspendDyn. Search \"DdnsStart\".\n\nAlso NOTE: `provider` httpGetEnv read but only used to advance a pointer — no validation of","stream":true,"block":0}

