data: {"seq":1433,"ts":"2026-08-22T19:31:25.854Z","text":"No page handler strings. The HTTP→struct filling may be done via a generic \"RpmFs\" mechanism (urlencoded params mapped by an XML schema). This architectural style means the chain entry in httpd is generic: POST /userRpm/NasSettingsRpm.htm with doType=... Actually the struct-filling is likely `httpRpmGetConfig(..., nasCfgTable, ...)` mapping param names to struct offsets at runtime (param table). Can't easily confirm the exact param name.\n\nGiven that, my call_chain can be: \n`POST /userRpm/Nas...(认证, doType=saveShareList&shareName=...) → httpd httpRpm参数表 → nas 配置结构(a1+80 shareName) → ucm IPC(127.0.0.1:51237) / 或 infra 通知 → uclited nasSambaSetShareList(0x4a63ec) → snprintf(\"rm -rf /tmp/samba/%s.smb.conf\", shareName) → system(0x4a63ec:29)`\n\nActually — even better: check who calls uclited nasSambaSetShareList with attacker input. Maybe there's a \"sw\" wrapper in uclited that is invoked from httpd directly via ucm op (two-step: httpd sets config (its own write) then sends \"restart\"/\"apply\" op). But uclited's nasSambaSetShareList in_degree=6 — 6 callers in uclited. Which of them is the ucm-triggered one? Likely a nas*ConfigSet op: \"nasSambaSrvStart\"?? nasSambaStart (0x4a44d0) calls execFormatCmd(\"smbd -D\") — smbd start. And nasSambaSetSysUser writes passwd. The \"save\" flow in uclited: ucm op 'nasSambaConfigSet' → nas cfg stored → call nasSambaSetShareList → system rm + restart samba (sub_4A4F08 probably calls nasSambaStop/Start).\n\nFor the finding, what matters: share name (attacker via auth) ends up in system() command. The intermediate exact function names: I know uclited's caller side partially: nasSambaStart/Stop, sub_4A4F08, sub_4A5EEC, sub_4A5704, sub_4A5AC4. And sub_4A5EEC(a1, name) builds share dir.\n\nAlso worth checking: does anything sanitize share name before storing? TP-Link web normally rejects some chars but this older firmware rarely. And can a share name even contain `;`? The web form allows most printable chars for \"share name\". I'll present it as post-auth RCE with default-credential precondition.\n\nSecond idea to strengthen dynamic evidence per orchestrator: the trace budget — fw_request_trace 70f79dca3ee7 (httpd DynDdnsRpm) is running; poll it. Also try one more trace for smbd/samba? samba_multicall md5 unknown. Let me poll the running trace now, and also look at whether uclited's other system() instances have similar injections: search sub_41153C (execFormatCmd's system wrapper) callers in uclited = functions calling execFormatCmd: nasSambaStart (\"smbd -D\" const), nasSamba...? \"swNasEjectDisk\" was httpd. uclited execFormatCmd callers: let me grep via search — \"execFormatCmd\" in uclited found only the function. Its callers unknown.\n\nAlso there's the sub_41153C callers... Let me look at uclited nasSambaSetUserList (0x4a4b48) — writes smbpasswd maybe via system with username! Let me read it + sub_4A4F08 (samba restart).","stream":true,"block":0}

