data: {"seq":1454,"ts":"2026-08-22T19:31:34.203Z","text":"JACKPOT — nasSambaSetUserList (uclited 0x4a4b48):\n\n```c\nexecFormatCmd(\"%s -p %s -a %s\", \"smbpasswd\", v1, v2)\n```\nwhere:\n- v1 = &a1[44 * a1[1] + 6] — **user name?** offset 44*idx+6 → at 44*(index)+6 dwords? a1 is int*, so a1[44*i+6] = dword at byte offset 176*i+24. Hmm, wait — a1[44*i+2] appears as username (myStrlwr lowercases it); a1[44*i+6] = **password** (the passwd value!). Let me map to the nasSambaSetSysUser: `v2 = myStrlwr(&a1[44 * i + 2], v10); v3 = myStrlwr(&a1[44 * i + 2], v10); fprintf(stream, fmt, v2, v3)` — that writes smbpasswd-file entries using the SAME field a1[44i+2] twice (as login and as passwd?). In SetUserList: `v1 = &a1[44*a1[1]+6]` (different field, offset +6 dwords = password field?) and `v2 = myStrlwr(&a1[44*a1[1]+2], v6)` (username field). So execFormatCmd(\"smbpasswd -p <password> -a <username>\",) — wait: \"%s -p %s -a %s\" with args (\"smbpasswd\", v1, v2) → `smbpasswd -p <v1=passwd> -a <v2=username>`. Both v1 and v2 are user-controlled strings (NAS account username/password configured on the web page)!\n\nexecFormatCmd = vsprintf(s[260]) + system! So:\n- **Command injection**: username/password containing `;`, `$()`, `` ` `` → injected into `smbpasswd -p ... -a ...` executed by /bin/sh as root. \n- **Stack overflow**: vsprintf into 260-byte buffer — a long username/password (>255) overflows.\n\nThis is the classic TP-Link NAS \"smbpasswd 命令注入\" — a real, citable, dangerous finding (post-auth admin → root RCE).\n\nAlso nasSambaSetShareList rm -rf system() with share name — second finding.\n\nBoth require admin auth (NAS settings). But 认证前提 is normal for router vuln databases and TP-Link default admin/admin. Reachability: post-auth → root RCE.\n\nAdditionally, check for an UNauthenticated route to these: the ucm IPC is loopback; the web is auth-gated. So unauth no.\n\nLet me also verify what user fields flow from WHERE into a1[44i+2]/[44i+6] in httpd: httpd nasSambaSetSysUser (0x546f24) presumably does similar strcpy/memcpy from struct — the struct in httpd is filled from POST params \"userName\"/\"passwd\" etc. But I don't have the param names. I can describe generically: \"NAS 用户/密码设置页\".\n\n","stream":true,"block":0}

