data: {"seq":1504,"ts":"2026-08-22T19:32:02.539Z","text":"F-mt4rye54-c344 recorded.\n\nnasFtpSetUserList: sprintf(v3[256], \"/tmp/vsftp/root/%s\", username) → **stack overflow** if username ≥ 234 chars (256-buffer; prefix 17-ish bytes","stream":true,"block":0}

event: thinking
data: {"seq":1505,"ts":"2026-08-22T19:32:02.906Z","text":"F-mt4rye54-c344 recorded.\n\nnasFtpSetUserList: sprintf(v3[256], \"/tmp/vsftp/root/%s\", username) → **stack overflow** if username ≥ 234 chars (256-buffer; prefix 17-ish bytes). sprintf unbounded into v3[256]! Username from config (auth). That's a stack overflow (CWE-121) — bounded nothing. Also writes vsftp passwd file with raw creds — vsftpd-format, not command exec. The overflow: sprintf(v3, \"/tmp/vsftp/root/%s\", name) — if name longer than ~238 → overflow. NAS username max via web is usually 32... but 用户名上限可能不严格。Still a weak trigger.\n\nWait, more interesting: is there a FTP module in httpd too (nasFtpSetUserList in httpd)? Possibly 0x54xxx. And vsftpd itself: does vsftpd use /tmp/vsftp/etc/passwd","stream":true,"block":0}

event: thinking
data: {"seq":1506,"ts":"2026-08-22T19:32:03.260Z","text":"F-mt4rye54-c344 recorded.\n\nnasFtpSetUserList: sprintf(v3[256], \"/tmp/vsftp/root/%s\", username) → **stack overflow** if username ≥ 234 chars (256-buffer; prefix 17-ish bytes). sprintf unbounded into v3[256]! Username from config (auth). That's a stack overflow (CWE-121) — bounded nothing. Also writes vsftp passwd file with raw creds — vsftpd-format, not command exec. The overflow: sprintf(v3, \"/tmp/vsftp/root/%s\", name) — if name longer than ~238 → overflow. NAS username max via web is usually 32... but 用户名上限可能不严格。Still a weak trigger.\n\nWait, more interesting: is there a FTP module in httpd too (nasFtpSetUserList in httpd)? Possibly 0x54xxx. And vsftpd itself: does vsftpd use /tmp/vsftp/etc/passwd with the \"user:pass:1:1;\" format? That's vsftpd's \"virtual user\" config with plaintext. And **vsftpd is a PUBLIC service (port 21/IN-012)**. The FTP accounts including \"tpsoholink\"/\"anon\"/\"guestanon\" plus user's own with a user-chosen password... but that","stream":true,"block":0}

