ckly confirm execFormatCmd's uclited caller count for the FTP user path: uclited nasFtpSetUserList doesn't execFormatCmd (only sprintf+mkdir). So FTP is overflow-only.\n\nLet me read uclited nasFtpCfgFileWrite full (v8 size) + httpd nasFtpSetUserList full (buffer size), and uclited nasFtpFolderAdd (share folder path → maybe execFormatCmd with foldername!). nasFtpFolderAdd (0x49ef54) — creates FTP share folder. If it does mkdir/system with folder name → injection. Read it.","stream":false,"block":0}

