data: {"seq":1634,"ts":"2026-08-22T19:33:32.548Z","text":"Both FTP user-list functions show `sprintf(s[256], \"/tmp/vsftp/root/%s\", username)` — 256-byte buffer, prefix 17 bytes → overflow needs username ≥ ~238 chars.\n\nBUT — one critical detail: the FTP structure field offsets DIFFER between httpd & uclited versions:\n- uclited nasFtpSetUserList: fprintf \"%s:%s:%d:%d;\" with username @ a1[44i+2], password @ a1[44i+6]\n- httpd nasFtpSetUserList: username @ a1[44i+2], password @ a1[44i+10]\n\nInteresting: In httpd's smbpasswd finding I used a1[44i+6] as password — same in both samba funcs (both used +6). OK.\n\nIs a ~238-char FTP username realistic? The web UI NAS username typically limited to ~16 chars. So the sprintf overflow isn't practically","stream":true,"block":0}

event: thinking
data: {"seq":1635,"ts":"2026-08-22T19:33:32.900Z","text":"Both FTP user-list functions show `sprintf(s[256], \"/tmp/vsftp/root/%s\", username)` — 256-byte buffer, prefix 17 bytes → overflow needs username ≥ ~238 chars.\n\nBUT — one critical detail: the FTP structure field offsets DIFFER between httpd & uclited versions:\n- uclited nasFtpSetUserList: fprintf \"%s:%s:%d:%d;\" with username @ a1[44i+2], password @ a1[44i+6]\n- httpd nasFtpSetUserList: username @ a1[44i+2], password @ a1[44i+10]\n\nInteresting: In httpd's smbpasswd finding I used a1[44i+6] as password — same in both samba funcs (both used +6). OK.\n\nIs a ~238-char FTP username realistic? The web UI NAS username typically limited to ~16 chars. So the sprintf overflow isn't practically triggerable unless the config can be set with a long string (cmdi via IPC? params come from web). Not strong — I'll skip recording FTP overflow to avoid noise; the two SMB injections remain the strong round-2 findings.\n\nLet me make sure I've done justice to the \"登录\" angle with one more concrete look — the actual login check.","stream":true,"block":0}

