data: {"seq":1652,"ts":"2026-08-22T19:33:39.436Z","text":"**KEY AUTH FINDING**: httpDispatcher: for each matched RPM handler (v6 != httpRpmFs && != httpHelpRequestRpm), it calls `sub_425CB8(a1, v6)`; **if sub_425CB8 returns non-zero → `return LoginRpmHtm(a1)`** — i.e., **redirect to login**! So sub_425CB8 is THE auth gate: whether the current session/request is authorized for that handler.\n\nAlso the unmatched URL case: `sub_425CB8(a1, v6)` with v6=0 (no matched handler) → GoIndex (redirect login). So all RPM handlers are gated by sub_425CB8. Login bypass = sub_425CB8 weakness, or finding an authenticated handler NOT in the RPM table (e.g., httpRpmFs paths or the file-server paths like /tmp/usbdisk, /var/diagno served via httpRpmFs!). The routes from arg_url (`/tmp/usbdisk/...`, `/var/...`, `/usr/libexec/sftp-server`) — what serves them? Probably the media/file httpmime paths which bypass sub_425CB8 (only RPM pages are gated).\n\nLet me read sub_425CB8 — the auth check — to find a bypass (e.g., \"Authorization\" cookie not validated when session flag set wrong, or session poisoning).","stream":false,"block":0}

