data: {"seq":1685,"ts":"2026-08-22T19:33:53.936Z","text":"VERY interesting:\n\n**sub_425460**: `httpAuthorizationGet(a1, 0)` — returns pointer to the Authorization header/cookie value. If it's `&httpNullByte` (no header → the special empty pointer), return **1 (=TRUE)**. Otherwise return (*v1 == 0) (value is empty string → TRUE).\n\n**sub_425AA4** flow when status != 200 (i.e., not the login page / not success):\n```c\nif ( sub_425460(a1) )       // auth header ABSENT or EMPTY → TRUE\n    goto LABEL_10;          // dword_5A51C0=3; return 2;\n```\nAnd in httpDispatcher: `v15 = sub_425CB8(a1, v6); if (v15) return LoginRpmHtm(a1);` — wait, return 2 from sub_425CB8 → v15=2 (truthy) → `return LoginRpmHtm(a1)` — DENIED → login page!! Hold on: sub_425AA4 returning 2 → sub_425CB8 returns 2 → httpDispatcher: `if (v15) return LoginRpmHtm(a1)` — YES it redirects to login. So return 2 = \"deny, show login\".\n\nRe-read: in httpDispatcher:\n```c\nv15 = sub_425CB8(a1, v6);\nv16 = v6;\nif ( v15 ) { ... return LoginRpmHtm(a1); }\n```\nSo ANY non-zero from sub_425CB8 → login page. sub_425CB8 returns: mode1: sub_425AA4's value. sub_425AA4: authenticated → return 1 → redirect to","stream":true,"block":0}

