data: {"seq":1690,"ts":"2026-08-22T19:33:55.968Z","text":"VERY interesting:\n\n**sub_425460**: `httpAuthorizationGet(a1, 0)` — returns pointer to the Authorization header/cookie value. If it's `&httpNullByte` (no header → the special empty pointer), return **1 (=TRUE)**. Otherwise return (*v1 == 0) (value is empty string → TRUE).\n\n**sub_425AA4** flow when status != 200 (i.e., not the login page / not success):\n```c\nif ( sub_425460(a1) )       // auth header ABSENT or EMPTY → TRUE\n    goto LABEL_10;          // dword_5A51C0=3; return 2;\n```\nAnd in httpDispatcher: `v15 = sub_425CB8(a1, v6); if (v15) return LoginRpmHtm(a1);` — wait, return 2 from sub_425CB8 → v15=2 (truthy) → `return LoginRpmHtm(a1)` — DENIED → login page!! Hold on: sub_425AA4 returning 2 → sub_425CB8 returns 2 → httpDispatcher: `if (v15) return LoginRpmHtm(a1)` — YES it redirects to login. So return 2 = \"deny, show login\".\n\nRe-read: in httpDispatcher:\n```c\nv15 = sub_425CB8(a1, v6);\nv16 = v6;\nif ( v15 ) { ... return LoginRpmHtm(a1); }\n```\nSo ANY non-zero from sub_425CB8 → login page. sub_425CB8 returns: mode1: sub_425AA4's value. sub_425AA4: authenticated → return 1 → redirect to login?? That contradicts...\n\nWait — maybe the semantics: sub_425CB8 returns 0 = OK (handler allowed), non-zero = need login. sub_425AA4: \n- sub_425104(v6) → 1 (session authed) → `dword_5A51C0=1; return 1;` — returns 1 → dispatch treats as \"show login\"??? That can't be right for an authenticated session...\n\nHmm. Look again at httpDispatcher: after v15=sub_425CB8(...): `if (v15) { return LoginRpmHtm(a1); }` — so nonzero → login. Then sub_425AA4 returning:\n- 1 (authed) → would show login — WRONG.\n...\n\nUnless sub_425CB8's return is inverted somewhere: Actually wait — maybe status==200 helps. A request that already passed login → the framework sets status 200 on the request object (the http status of the page?). When authed: sub_425AA4 returns 1 → login page shown?? No...\n\nHmm, actually let me recheck: in the else-branch of httpDispatcher, `v17 = v16(a1);` — v16 is the handler — but only reached if v15==0. For an authenticated session, sub_425104 returns 1 → sub_425AA4 `return 1` → v15=1 → LoginRpmHtm. Contradiction → my reading of dispatch must be wrong.\n\nLook again at httpDispatcher loop:\n```\nv15 = sub_425CB8(a1, v6);\nv16 = v6;\nif ( v15 ) { printf(...); return LoginRpmHtm(a1); }\nv17 = v16(a1);\n```\nYes: v15 truthy → LoginRpmHtm. So sub_425CB8 must return 0 for \"let handler run\". Then:\n- sub_425AA4: authed → return 1 → login?! \n\nWait, maybe I misordered: `sub_425104(v6)` returns 1 for authed; then `dword_5A51C0=1; return 1;` → shows login. That makes no sense... UNLESS the return path is: `return 1` means \"yes, show login\" is wrong and the code actually uses it as \"handled-skip\". Let me recheck the alternative path: status != 200, sub_425460 (no auth header) true → LABEL_10 → return 2 → login page (matches: no auth header → show login). And status == 200 && handler==LoginRpmHtm → return 0 → allow LoginRpmHtm run. status==","stream":true,"block":0}

