data: {"seq":2238,"ts":"2026-08-22T19:46:35.293Z","text":"ucm_trans_ioctl → sub_420BCC → op handlers. The chain: ucm_cfg_handler → ucm_trans_ioctl → sub_420BCC (opcode table dispatch) → nasSambaSetUserList/nasSambaSetShareList. Good enough — chain closed with the exact function addresses for the SMB findings:\n`httpd nasSambaSetUserList... ` hmm wait — actually the uclited ops that call these nas functions are triggered from httpd via ucm when the httpd handler processes \"Save\" — httpd's OWN handlers also run nasSambaSetUserList directly (0x5471d0 in httpd calls execFormatCmd!). So BOTH binaries execute the smbpasswd injection independently.\n\nChain for F-mt4rye54-c344 (httpd variant): `/userRpm/NasFolderSharingRpm.htm` accountSave → (nas_admin_name/nas_admin_pwd at s[64]/s[68]) → swNasSetSrvUserList → uclited ... Actually httpd nasSambaSetUserList called from httpd's swNasSrvStart/SetSrvUserList... Whatever — chain already recorded with NAS page → nasSambaSetUserList → execFormatCmd. Good.\n\nvsftpd fuzz still running. Poll again in a bit.\n\nActually, let me reconsider what remains for \"主要攻击面扫完\" status:\nCovered: httpd (DDNS/ping/auth/NAS/login infra), minidlna (HTTP/SSDP/XML), dhcp6c/dhcp6s (UDP/ctl/options), uclited (IPC/wlan/NAS/FTP/DOS), xl2tpd, ipcserver, bpalogin(prev finding), vsftpd (static partial + fuzz in progress), dropbear/samba_multicall (not decompiled — only fuzz possible).\n\nRemaining actionable: poll vsftpd fuzz to ok; maybe start another fuzz on smbd? I don't have smbd md5... samba_multicall md5 unknown. vsftpd fuzz is the main in-flight item.\n\nLet me poll vsftpd fuzz again and, if still running, look at one more vsftpd static point: the custom TP-Link check_passwd (0x41470c getPasswdInfo aside) — actually find where vsftpd validates virtual users: search \"check_user\" or \"auth_pass\"... vsftpd handle_auth at 0x41d518 is a no-op? Let me read handle_auth + ftp_getline + the \"passwd file\" opener (vsf_sysutil_getcwd?) Hmm. Actually for vsftpd, the risky part in TP-Link ports is the **custom passwd check on FTP USER/PASS with the /tmp/vsftp/etc/passwd format \"user:pwd:1:1;\"** — if it parses with strtok/strncpy into fixed buffers → overflow pre-auth! Search vsftpd functions named \"parseUser\"/\"checkUser\"... search \"vsf_conf_get_res\"... skip; poll fuzz instead.","stream":false,"block":0}

