data: {"seq":2285,"ts":"2026-08-22T19:47:00.044Z","text":"httpSetVirtualPath — session validation for the \"virtual path\" requests (probably the \"Save\"... Actually this parses the URL path component used for login URL: the login token is embedded in the URL (/TOKEN17chars/...). It checks:\n- dword_5E69E4 == 2 (logged-in mode)\n- sub_4255C8(a1) (MAC/IP match)\n- a2 == strchr(a2, '/') — a2 starts with '/'\n- strcmp(a2, \"/\")\n- strlen(a2+1) >= 0x11 (17)\n- if strncmp(v2+1, byte_5E69E8, 0x10) == 0 → session_valid → dword_5C1B30=1, v2 += 17.\n\nSo byte_5E69E8 = the session token (16 bytes, set at login via sub_425838 8-char random + pad). Clients authenticated by embedding the token in URL path after login! And dword_5C1B30 = \"session active\" flag.\n\nLogin gate summary:\n- After correct password → server sets byte_5E69E8 (random token) and mode=2... wait — but the PASSWORD CHECK itself: where? login POST → LoginRpmHtm? The password check is where byte_5E69E8 gets SET, which was sub_425838 called from sub_42595C when a2==LoginRpmHtm and dword_5C1B30 false →","stream":true,"block":0}

