data: {"seq":2369,"ts":"2026-08-22T19:47:47.435Z","text":"AS-010 has no md5 (samba not decompiled). smbpasswd is a CLIENT tool, actually, not a listener — the identification's gate misfired (bpalogin-style client misclassification; smbpasswd is the samba password utility, invoked with -a etc, not a TCP daemon). smbpasswd md5 not given anyway.\n\nSo samba_multicall/smbd/dropbear md5s are not present in the graph (未反编译 → md5 unknown to me). Without md5, can't fuzz them via fw_request_fuzz (requires manifest md5). Let me check the identification full document for md5s? identification.json didn't include md5 per binary. The binary md5s come from decompiled modules only.\n\nHmm —","stream":true,"block":0}

