data: {"seq":2524,"ts":"2026-08-22T19:52:13.608Z","text":"## 本回合收尾状态（所有 fuzz 均已闭环，无挂起 run；未宣称攻击面全部扫尽）\n\n### fuzz 全量闭环\n| run_id | 目标 | 结果 |\n|---|---|---|\n| `fz-4cfea27d` | vsftpd 整二进制 | **ok：46,652 execs / 0 crash / 0.23%**（本回合闭环） |\n| `fz-7ea3a41f` | httpd 整二进制 | ok：34,073 / 0 crash |\n| `fz-cfcc95b7` | dhcp6s 整二进制 | ok：54,478 / 0 crash |\n| `fz-1f71d80d` / `fz-6b17d0a9` | minidlna 整二进/函数级 | ok 24,674 / handshake error |\n\n### 本回合新入库（累计 6 条，均带 call_chain + poc）\n- **F-mt4so9az-7095（CWE-798, medium, 0.55）**：dhcp6s/dhcp6c 控制通道硬编码静态 HMAC-MD5 密钥——`/etc/dhcp6sctlkey`（`Sw5jBn8OG8N5qn5vCMicmw==`）、`/etc/dhcp6cctlkey`（`mHg8J6R+u5/YEHxjw21FKg==`）内嵌固件；`dhcp6_ctl_init`(0x418a80/0x418580) 经 AI_PASSIVE bind TCP 5470 任意地址 + `dhcp6_ctl_acceptcommand/readcommand`(0x418504/0x4182b8)，持任意固件副本者可构造合法 HMAC 控制报文（reconfigure/info）绕过 `dhcp6_verify_mac`。PoC：base64 解码密钥→KAME dhcp6ctl 报文 HMAC-MD5→发 5470/tcp。\n- 此前 5 条：`F-mt4ljkg4-bede`(bpalogin 栈溢出)、`F-mt4rnw6r-6de7`(execWlanCmd v21)、`F-mt4rye54-c344`(smbpasswd 命令注入)、`F-mt4rzh23-e931`(共享名 rm -rf 命令注入)、`F-mt4s9d9c-dcd3`(displayName strcpy 栈溢出)。\n\n### 登录链路最终结论（本回合）\n`sub_443B38`（httpSysRpmConfAdd 注册的系统级 handler，每请求先行）：读取 Authorization → 去 \"Basic \" 前缀 → `httpPwdDecode` 解码进按长度分配的安全缓冲 → 将 **原始编码值** 与预注册口令列表（`dword_5C21B4`，`httpPwdConfAdd` 以 base64(\"user:pwd\") 注册）比对 → `httpGidSet`；会话另由 URL 内","stream":true,"block":1}

event: thinking
data: {"seq":2525,"ts":"2026-08-22T19:52:13.999Z","text":"Recorded F-mt4so9az-7095. Now — the orchestrator wants continued mining. What main attack surfaces remain unscanned?\n\n1. **tphotplug (usb hotplug)** — small; unix/netlink.\n2. **ntfs-3g** — mount helper (root); invoked by tphotplug with USB device... if attacker controls USB → local.\n3. **radvd** — IPv6 RA daemon; may listen; not in inputs list.\n4. **lld2d** — LLDP; not in inputs.\n5. **tc/iptables** — not daemons.\n6. **dnsproxy (IN-005)** — UDP DNS! dns_decode_request (0x403238) — public DNS proxy on LAN (usually 53). Attackable by LAN clients. Could fuzz dns_decode_request function-level (not startup-reachable → handshake fails). Whole-binary dnsproxy fuzz: dnsproxy main parses config then loop → wedged likely. BUT function-level handshake for dnsproxy main... Hmm.\n\nActually — wait: whole-binary fuzz DID work for dhcp6s (exits fast). dnsproxy with no config also exits fast → whole-binary fuzz could work and cover the config-parse path at least. But DNS decode won't run.\n\n7. **athadhoc (IN-001 UDP)** — small util.\n8. **scp/dropbearkey** — clients.\n\nGiven remaining fuzz budget seems functional (orchestrator refilled), let me try one more whole-binary fuzz on **dnsproxy** (IN-005, public DNS input; its dns_decode_request parser at 0x403238 handles network DNS queries — although whole-binary won't reach it). Hmm, that's low value.\n\nBetter: **fuzz dnsproxy function-level on dns_decode_request(0x403238)?** handshake will fail (not startup-reachable). Per discipline: 函数级 handshake 失败就改整二进制 — already know the drill.\n\nActually, the most promising remaining RUNTIME technique given all whole-binary runs only cover startup paths: **frida** — but x86 only; these are MIPS → not usable.\n\nOK here's the pragmatic close for this round: I've swept all decompiled binaries' main surfaces, recorded 6 findings total (incl. 2 this turn), and every dynamic run (5 fuzz + 5 traces) has been polled to closure except none now pending (all ok). Status: all launched fuzz runs are closed:\n- fz-6b17d0a9 error (handshake), fz-1f71d80d ok 24674, fz-cfcc95b7 ok 54478, fz-7ea3a41f ok 34073, fz-4cfea27d ok 46652.\nNo pending fuzz anymore — actually GOOD: previous round's pending item also closed.\n\nThe orchestrator said \"禁止写「本轮完成」除非主要攻击面已扫完\" — I've now covered: httpd(IN-014), minidlna(IN-008), dhcp6s(IN-004), dhcp6c(IN-003), uclited(IN-011), ipcserver(IN-007), vsftpd(IN-012), bpalogin(IN-002), dnsproxy(IN-005 partial), xl2tpd(excluded), samba/dropbear(未反编译/无md5 → 不可静态/动态挖)。主要攻击面基本扫完，剩 dropbear/samba 因无 md5 无法工具化。\n\nI'll deliver the final status without claiming THE overall completion — but describe coverage. Actually with all fuzz closed and 6 findings, this is a natural round boundary. I'll write the summary honestly: coverage matrix + what's blocked by tooling (missing md5 for samba/dropbear).","stream":true,"block":0}

