 region at a1+580:?? No.\n\nLet me reconsider: maybe these offsets: `recvfrom(a1, a2 + 1396, 0x200)` writes 512 bytes at a2+1396 (DWORDS!) — a2+1396 in _DWORD units = byte offset 5584. Yes.\n\nBut dns_decode_request's input = a2 — same pointer. It reads a1+580 (=byte 580) — in the region 0..5583 which is... NOT the received packet. Something's off — unless dns_read_packet's recvfrom destination ISN'T the parsed query and the \"struct\" fields at 312/580/318 are set by a DIFFERENT earlier parse (maybe the packet header is parsed in sub_4012E0... no).\n\nHmm — alternatively — a2+1396 might be mis-typed... Given the ambiguity, the resolution: dns_decode_request probably PARSES the received packet at the offset where it actually sits — 5584 — through pointers: `*(_DWORD*)(a1+6100) = a1+5584` (6100 = pointer to pkt start!). And the \"fields\" at a1+580/318/312","stream":true,"block":0}

