data: {"seq":2744,"ts":"2026-08-22T20:01:31.677Z","text":"sub_41D224 = the mini-XML SAX parser (callbacks at a1+24/28/32 for tag/content). All cursor operations bounded by a1+4 (end pointer) — bounds-checked. No allocation, uses callbacks. Safe-ish. No recordable bug.\n\nidentification full didn't give md5s either (no manifest md5). So smbd/dropbear remain md5-less.\n\nOK — I've now swept: athadhoc (IN-001) not yet touched! It's UDP, 200 somethings? Let me check athadhoc — it's the ad-hoc WiFi control daemon (UDP). Not decompiled? It's in identification IN-001 with processing chain but AS-001 says \"final_handler unresolved (static-only)\". Let me look at AS-001 quickly... might be decompiled. Also bpalogin done.\n\nAlternatives to keep the round productive:\n1. Read AS-001 (athadhoc) to see md5/entry; if decompiled, check for bugs; if not, stop.\n2. Mine dnsproxy further? The 1-byte underflow is weak.\n3. Mine uclited more: it has dispatch_chain noting uclited spawns dnsproxy/udhcpd/udhcpc/dhcp6s/dhcp6ctl/radvd/tphotplug — the \"spawn/exec candidates\" — meaning uclited system()-launches these! If any of those launches interpolate attacker strings → new cmdi. Let me search uclited for \"system(\" with these binary names: search \"udhcpc\" in uclited → find exec function. udhcpc/dnsproxy launches happen when WAN settings applied — the WAN config comes from POST; if uclited builds \"udhcpc -i %s\" with interface name from config → injection? Interface names are restricted (ath0/eth0.2 etc via dropdown mostly). Also \"dhcp6s\" launch is like \"dhcp6s -c /tmp/dhcp6s.conf %s\" with interface. And \"radvd\". Let me search uclited for system-with-path strings: search \"udhcpd\" / \"udhcpc\" patterns.","stream":false,"block":0}

