data: {"seq":2754,"ts":"2026-08-22T20:01:38.184Z","text":"No direct function names for those spawns. The spawns are probably via execFormatCmd with filesystem path strings in .rodata (constants + maybe interface arg from config).\n\nGiven diminishing returns and the explicit instruction \"不要写本轮完成除非攻击面扫完\", I should keep working on whatever is open. Options remaining that are actionable:\n\nA) Request a TRACE for dnsproxy (UDP 53, qemu) — probably refused (UDP not HTTP), but it demonstrates dynamic attempt on IN-005. Trace budget was ~13 used; may 429. Try — cheap.\n\nB) Read AS-001 (athadhoc) — one more input surface.\n\nC) The sub_4028D8 1-byte underflow on empty qname — let me double check the exploitability reasoning: writing 1 byte BEFORE a1 (the request struct start). a1 = &v6[0] (sp+48). v6[-1] = byte at sp+47 — part of the stack frame of sub_401B38 (adjacent to timeout struct? timeout at sp+40..47!). Actually v6 is at sp+48; timeout (struct timeval, 8 bytes) at sp+40; the byte at sp+47 = last byte of timeout.tv_usec. Writing 1 byte there — modifies timeout.tv_usec low byte. Then... select uses timeout locally (1s/0us). The write happens inside sub_4015B","stream":true,"block":0}

