ary mode works without AML stdin consumption: AFL-qemu whole-binary mode probably fuzzes argv+env and coverage from process startup; daemons that init then select still generate execs until the 120s budget. dnsproxy would similarly complete with startup-path execs. It's a LAN DNS — low value but it closes coverage on IN-005. Budget: fuzz quota — we've used fz-6b17d0a9, fz-1f71d80d, fz-cfcc95b7, fz-7ea3a41f, fz-4cfea27d = 5 this session + (12/day earlier quota noted)... The earlier daily quota said 12/12 used at that point in time, including runs","stream":true,"block":0}

