data: {"seq":2953,"ts":"2026-08-22T20:06:35.335Z","text":"- **dnsproxy fuzz fz-e9c6553e: ok, 57,855 execs / 0 crash / 0.05%** — all fuzz runs now closed.\n- pppd is its own binary (b4483e71), spawned likely by uclited or by shell. pppDnsGet (uclited/httpd) reads DNS via fscanf from a ppp file — file-based, not exec. The PPPoE username/password → where does pppd get them? Via /tmp/ppp/options or environment (CALLER_ID?). xl2tpd's start_pppd set env CALLER_ID. For PPPoE, this firmware... The router PPPoE client: likely udhcpc? no. pppd? Archer C7 PPPoE: nt pppd invoked by... maybe uclited writes /tmp/ppp/options.pppoe with user/passwd. If written via fprintf and pppd reads it — no shell involved → no cmdi (config-file injection into pppd options could add \"pty\" etc — post-auth escalation only).\n\nAt this point every fuzz run is closed: httpd 34,073 / dhcp6s 54,478 / minidlna 24,674 / vsftpd 46,652 / dnsproxy 57,855 — total ~217k execs, 0 crashes.\n\nFor this round's deliverable I should produce a final consolidated account of the full campaign. The orchestrator says \"禁止写「本轮完成」除非主要攻击面已扫完\" — the honest position: the *tool-accessible* attack surface has now been swept: all IN-xxx inputs analyzed (httpd, uclited, minidlna, dhcp6c/s, vsftpd, dnsproxy, athadhoc, bpalogin, ipcserver(unix), dnsproxy) plus excluded-but-scored (xl2tpd falsified). Remaining: smbd/dropbear (not decompiled/no md5 — genuinely blocked), full-system emulation for post-auth verification.\n\nI'll give the consolidated campaign summary with the 6 findings and the exhaustive per-surface verdict table, plus the exact remaining blockers — and I will NOT use the \"完成\" phrase.","stream":true,"block":0}

