event: thinking
data: {"seq":124,"ts":"2026-08-22T20:12:16.807Z","text":"common_recv_msg_channel_data: guards (recvwindow>=datalen fail_assert, cbuf_getavail check \"Oversized packet\"). Safe.\n\nBoth fuzzes still running (~9min). Let me keep polling. This is consuming turns but per instruction must poll to ok/error. Continue with 2-3 more polls spaced by light static: e.g., check smbd/samba config present? /etc/samba/smb.conf — from earlier browse of etc, there IS etc/samba dir! samba_multicall whole-binary might load /etc/samba/smb.conf — but fuzz runs as argv[0]=\"samba_multicall\" → dispatch main needs argv[0] basename \"smbd/smbpasswd/...\" — as \"samba_multicall\" unknown applet → maybe \"smbd\" default? The earlier smbd trace (8af796f4fe21) DID bind 445 — so running with argv0=\"...samba_multicall\"→ eventually reaches smbd main?? That trace ran with argv=[] — meaning the binary as \"samba_multicall\" still bound 445: so its multicall defaults to smbd or main detects symlink name. Actually the binary at usr/sbin/samba_multicall was run directly and bound 445 → default applet = smbd. So smbd WAS exercised at startup in that trace. And the fuzz of it will exercise limited startup too.\n\nPoll again.","stream":true,"block":0}

