event: thinking
data: {"seq":171,"ts":"2026-08-22T20:12:45.555Z","text":"Both fuzzes still running after ~20min. This is longer than previous daemons (httpd/vsftpd/dnsproxy flipped by ~15-20 min wall). These two could be queued waiting for a free worker (only one fuzz worker might run at a time; I ran both concurrently — they may serialize). The platform may execute them sequentially — the second starts only after the first finishes. That means total wall time = 2× (~2min AFL + queue). I must keep polling.\n\nTo avoid pure-poll wastefulness, do a static check in between: the smbd side — since trace 8af796f4fe21 proves smbd binds 445 and runs in qemu, maybe I can get a handle on smbd parsing via the **smb.conf path**: smbd reads /etc/samba/smb.conf; from the earlier fw_browse of etc, there's a samba dir. If smb.conf exists with a suspicious share pointing to /tmp/usbdisk, SMB share access... not recordable without dynamic SMB.\n\nLet me also review one more worth-documenting item: **dropbear trace failed due to host port 22 in use** — that's an","stream":true,"block":0}

event: thinking
data: {"seq":172,"ts":"2026-08-22T20:12:45.928Z","text":"Both fuzzes still running after ~20min. This is longer than previous daemons (httpd/vsftpd/dnsproxy flipped by ~15-20 min wall). These two could be queued waiting for a free worker (only one fuzz worker might run at a time; I ran both concurrently — they may serialize). The platform may execute them sequentially — the second starts only after the first finishes. That means total wall time = 2× (~2min AFL + queue). I must keep polling.\n\nTo avoid pure-poll wastefulness, do a static check in between: the smbd side — since trace 8af796f4fe21 proves smbd binds 445 and runs in qemu, maybe I can get a handle on smbd parsing via the **smb.conf path**: smbd reads /etc/samba/smb.conf; from the earlier fw_browse of etc, there's a samba dir. If smb.conf exists with a suspicious share pointing to /tmp/usbdisk, SMB share access... not recordable without dynamic SMB.\n\nLet me also review one more worth-documenting item: **dropbear trace failed due to host port 22 in use** — that's an environment limitation; a retry would fail identically. Document.\n\nKeep polling.","stream":true,"block":0}

