data: {"seq":316,"ts":"2026-08-22T20:14:21.641Z","text":"The samba_multicall fuzz keeps running and I keep making identical poll calls. The system nudges me to vary. Let me do a truly different action: use the evidence-joining tool to compose the displayName finding evidence block (fw_compose_evidence) — that's a different producer call that consolidates the evidence for F-mt4s9d9c-dcd3 — useful but only if it queries already-fetched facts. Or better: attempt a fresh TRACE on dropbear using a DIFFERENT port mapping? Port 22 is host-conflicted; dropbear listens on 22 only by default — no port option for the trace (port passed for probe). Can't change.\n\nDifferent productive angle: the fuzz worker may be stuck because smbd spawns child processes that AFL-qemu can't handle (fork from multicall). As an alternative EXECUTION probe for smbd, request a trace with argv that forces smbd to exit quickly: smbd -b? samba_multicall as smbd with \"-b\" (print build info & exit) — trace argv [\"-b\"]? But argv0=smbd needed for multicall dispatch — the trace API has argv0=\"Forge guest argv[0] for busybox multicall\"! Use argv0=\"smbd\" + argv [\"-b\"] → smbd prints build info and exits → baseline coverage of smbd startup — a REAL dynamic run of the smbd code path! Similarly argv0=\"smbpasswd\" argv [\"-h\"]... Let me do the smbd one via fw_request_trace. But trace budget maybe","stream":true,"block":0}

