M UI restricts but the HTTP handler strncpy's accountSave user to 16 bytes (s[64] strncpy 0x10). For the FTP user list the source is the same config — plausibly enforced. So the overflow is not triggerable with normal input — correctly kept out.\n\nDecision: this turn = dropbear auth depth (done, no vuln), samba fuzz closed earlier, wrap with a status note listing precisely what's left and why (not \"完成\"). But the orchestrator says don't stop... The system might keep looping. To make genuine progress I'll do one more real verification: re-attempt dropbear trace (port 22) in case the host port freed — cheap and directly requested by the orchestrator's guidance (they said non-HTTP ports omit request_path; port 22 → TCP probe). If it fails again with the bind conflict, that's documented evidence. Also poll nothing (no running fuzz left). Let me also try vsftpd-style: dropbear argv0=\"dropbear\" argv [\"-F\"] (foreground, no daemon) — under qemu it would bind 22 (host conflict anyway on the tracer side? the tracer binds the HOST port to forward... the failure was binding host 127.0.0.1:22 — inherent). Skip retry.\n\nActually one NEW idea for smbd protocol-level static: smbd is not decompiled, but I can check smbd's CONFIG that the firmware ships: /etc/samba/smb.conf — browse it; and check whether it's the nasFtp-style \"share\" with \"guest ok\" — earlier I dropped this. Let me finally read etc/samba/smb.conf (firmware default) to close the guest-exposure question with evidence — quick + factual.","stream":true,"block":0}

