data: {"seq":322,"ts":"2026-08-22T20:23:40.285Z","text":"athadhoc fuzz still running (~3 min, small binary — should finish soon). Instead of repeating the poll, do a distinct useful action now and poll again after: e.g., re-verify one detail of the newest finding F-mt4tq5ud-30c1 — the s[1601] offset semantics. In ff_rtsp_connect, s = _DWORD s[1716]; s[1601] byte offset = 6404; s[1617] = 6468 (\"WMServer/\" check at s[1617] → byte 6468). These are inside the parsed-reply struct (ff_rtsp_parse_reply writes \"public\" at offset 6404??). Can't fully confirm semantics, but the code plainly shows strcpy(dest[64], &s[1601]) with s the OPTIONS reply buffer — dest overflow is code-verified regardless of which header it maps to. OK.\n\nAlso: quickly check whether minidlna even links an RTSP demuxer with protocol registration — search minidlna module for \"rtsp\" string-ref functions: search \"rtsp\" in minidlna.","stream":true,"block":0}

