data: {"seq":696,"ts":"2026-08-22T20:35:29.351Z","text":"sub_414334 is the EVENT subscription NOTIFY generator (builds event property-set XML), NOT the request-arg parser! It builds a small notify message. So getVarsContentDirectory returns the event document (used for subscription events), not the POST request parser. My assumption was wrong — this is the genVars direction.\n\nThe actual SOAP REQUEST argument parser is different: in stock minidlna, POST requests parse the body via `shd = xmlParseGetVar...`... Also note: the event property-set builder iterates a var table — the \"_DWORD* a1\" = buffer (malloc 0x200=512). All sub_412D00 appends bounded by &size — safe. But: `v3[*a1] = 0` sets NUL at position *a1 — the buffer (512 alloc) with size limit 512 — if *a1==512 exactly → 1-byte OOB write at v5[512]. sub_412D00 appends with max size 512 (size_t*). If the generated content >= 512, *a1 could hit 512 → NUL one byte past malloc(512) → **1-byte heap OOB write**. But content is static names + one value — tiny (<200B). Not triggerable. Skip.\n\nOK the real request parse: since the SOAP table off_4714D4 handlers (Browse","stream":true,"block":0}

