data: {"seq":722,"ts":"2026-08-22T20:35:43.775Z","text":"call_trace empty. Different approach — search for the strings used in Browse SQL to find the builder: search pattern \"OBJECTS\" or \"OBJECT_ID\" in minidlna module (string refs appear in function names? No—only if the string constant is exported as a symbol like a label). Search \"OBJECT\" pattern in minidlna limited: might surface a function named by string? Probably not.\n\nGiven the limits, the honest conclusion on minidlna objectID: the handler chain table is rodata (unreadable via tools), named symbols absent, SQL builder not locatable. In the UPSTREAM code for this minidlna version (1.1.x), BrowseDirectChildren and SearchRequest parse ObjectID/ContainerID via atoi → numeric-safe; SearchCriteria is NOT used in SQL for SearchRequests in most builds (criteria only for \"MEDIA\" browsed?). So no SQL injection in known minidlna behavior. I've spent enough; the minidlna SOAP SQL-injection question is investigated to the tool boundary: no evidence of injection","stream":true,"block":0}

