data: {"seq":723,"ts":"2026-08-22T20:35:44.174Z","text":"call_trace empty. Different approach — search for the strings used in Browse SQL to find the builder: search pattern \"OBJECTS\" or \"OBJECT_ID\" in minidlna module (string refs appear in function names? No—only if the string constant is exported as a symbol like a label). Search \"OBJECT\" pattern in minidlna limited: might surface a function named by string? Probably not.\n\nGiven the limits, the honest conclusion on minidlna objectID: the handler chain table is rodata (unreadable via tools), named symbols absent, SQL builder not locatable. In the UPSTREAM code for this minidlna version (1.1.x), BrowseDirectChildren and SearchRequest parse ObjectID/ContainerID via atoi → numeric-safe; SearchCriteria is NOT used in SQL for SearchRequests in most builds (criteria only for \"MEDIA\" browsed?). So no SQL injection in known minidlna behavior. I've spent enough; the minidlna SOAP SQL-injection question is investigated to the tool boundary: no evidence of injection, upstream behavior numeric-safe. I will NOT file a speculative finding.\n\nNext: uclited unscanned handlers per orchestrator. What uclited set-functions remain unexamined? Let me pick the biggest: uclited in ftp/samba share path done; the **\"Execute","stream":true,"block":0}

event: thinking
data: {"seq":724,"ts":"2026-08-22T20:35:44.560Z","text":"call_trace empty. Different approach — search for the strings used in Browse SQL to find the builder: search pattern \"OBJECTS\" or \"OBJECT_ID\" in minidlna module (string refs appear in function names? No—only if the string constant is exported as a symbol like a label). Search \"OBJECT\" pattern in minidlna limited: might surface a function named by string? Probably not.\n\nGiven the limits, the honest conclusion on minidlna objectID: the handler chain table is rodata (unreadable via tools), named symbols absent, SQL builder not locatable. In the UPSTREAM code for this minidlna version (1.1.x), BrowseDirectChildren and SearchRequest parse ObjectID/ContainerID via atoi → numeric-safe; SearchCriteria is NOT used in SQL for SearchRequests in most builds (criteria only for \"MEDIA\" browsed?). So no SQL injection in known minidlna behavior. I've spent enough; the minidlna SOAP SQL-injection question is investigated to the tool boundary: no evidence of injection, upstream behavior numeric-safe. I will NOT file a speculative finding.\n\nNext: uclited unscanned handlers per orchestrator. What uclited set-functions remain unexamined? Let me pick the biggest: uclited in ftp/samba share path done; the **\"ExecuteDmzCfg\" (httpd) done; uclited ExecuteDmzCfg (0x431b84)** — NOT read yet! uclited's own DMZ builder may sprintf+system with DMZ host IP (numeric, safe) — check quickly to close. Also **ExecuteStaticRouteTable (0x43fd18)/","stream":true,"block":0}

event: thinking
data: {"seq":725,"ts":"2026-08-22T20:35:44.921Z","text":"call_trace empty. Different approach — search for the strings used in Browse SQL to find the builder: search pattern \"OBJECTS\" or \"OBJECT_ID\" in minidlna module (string refs appear in function names? No—only if the string constant is exported as a symbol like a label). Search \"OBJECT\" pattern in minidlna limited: might surface a function named by string? Probably not.\n\nGiven the limits, the honest conclusion on minidlna objectID: the handler chain table is rodata (unreadable via tools), named symbols absent, SQL builder not locatable. In the UPSTREAM code for this minidlna version (1.1.x), BrowseDirectChildren and SearchRequest parse ObjectID/ContainerID via atoi → numeric-safe; SearchCriteria is NOT used in SQL for SearchRequests in most builds (criteria only for \"MEDIA\" browsed?). So no SQL injection in known minidlna behavior. I've spent enough; the minidlna SOAP SQL-injection question is investigated to the tool boundary: no evidence of injection, upstream behavior numeric-safe. I will NOT file a speculative finding.\n\nNext: uclited unscanned handlers per orchestrator. What uclited set-functions remain unexamined? Let me pick the biggest: uclited in ftp/samba share path done; the **\"ExecuteDmzCfg\" (httpd) done; uclited ExecuteDmzCfg (0x431b84)** — NOT read yet! uclited's own DMZ builder may sprintf+system with DMZ host IP (numeric, safe) — check quickly to close. Also **ExecuteStaticRouteTable (0x43fd18)/executeDhcpStaticRoute (0x4401ac)** — newtork routing iptables builders with... router IPs & interfaces — interfaces like \"ath0\"/\"br0\" from config (choices), IPs numeric. Check ExecuteDmzCfg uclited quickly, then static route table — for any","stream":true,"block":0}

