data: {"seq":857,"ts":"2026-08-22T20:38:22.017Z","text":"**pppoeFormatCmd analysis (uclited 0x448d14)**:\n\nThe PPPoE command is built in `a2` (byte_5448E4 global) as `\"pppd pppoe ...\"` + suffixes, then `system(a2)` runs it. Fields interpolated:\n- rp_pppoe_ac: (a1+544) string — PPPoE AC name (from config) ✓ String!\n- rp_pppoe_service: (a1+512) string — Service name ✓ String!\n- ifname: getWanStaticIpIfName() ✓ String\n- unit/noaccomp/... numbers\n- user_len/passwd_len numbers\n- mru/mtu numbers\n- inet_ntoa IP\n- lcp-echo numbers\n\n**BUT the PPPoE username/password are NOT put in the command line** — they go to /tmp/pppoe_auth_info_ipv4 (user/pass via vnet_functions fill → v20/v21 → fwrite). The pppd reads them from the file (user_len/passwd_len + special-flag report lengths). So credential injection is via FILE (used by pppd's own parsing — pppd reads the file, not shell) — not shell-injectable.\n\nThe shell-injectable STRING fields: `rp_pppoe_ac` (a1+544, AC name) and `rp_pppoe_service` (a1+512, service name) — from PPPoECfgRpm advanced settings (authenticated web config). If AC/service names from config contain `;` or shell metacharacters → **command injection into system(byte_5448E4) as root**. AC name & service name are arbitrary strings in the PPPoE advanced config page (no validation typically!). THIS is a smbpasswd-family command injection on the WAN PPPoE config — same class as the NAS injections but for PPPoE dial-up!\n\nAlso: `strcpy(a2,...)` then repeated `sprintf(&a2[offset], ...)` without length check — a2=byte_5448E4 is a GLOBAL buffer of unknown size (probably 512/1024); AC(≤?)/service(≤?) names from config with length limits (web limits to ~64?) — stack/global overflow if not enforced. But web likely limits AC/service lengths. The injection doesn't need length.\n\nTrigger: authenticated user sets PPPoE AC name to `x;telnetd -l /bin/sh;` → save → dial (pppoeCmdReqIPv4 on link up / re-dial) → system(\"pppd pppoe rp_pppoe_ac x;telnetd...\") → RCE.\n\nThis is a NEW, clean, code-verified finding: **CWE-78 command injection via PPPoE AC/Service name (uclited pppoeFormatCmd → system)**.\n\nChain: `/userRpm/PPPoECfgAdvRpm.htm`(认证) → swPppoe 配置(uclited 配置存储 v5) → pppoeCmdReq(0x4484d0)/pppoeCmdReqIPv4(0x4488f4) → pppoeFormatCmd(0x448d14) → sprintf 拼接 `rp_pppoe_ac %s`/`rp_pppoe_service %s`（AC/Service 名未转义） → system(byte_5448E4)。\n\nRecord it now as finding #8. binary: uclited d61e67ed; function 0x448d14 pppoeFormatCmd. severity","stream":true,"block":0}

