data: {"seq":933,"ts":"2026-08-22T20:39:55.752Z","text":"Parse callbacks analysis:\n\nsub_41C5B0 (tag cb): \n- n = min(a3, 63); memcpy(a1+1, a2, n) — copies tag name into a1+4 (the parent struct's 64-byte \"current tag\" buffer: a1 = &list-entry's tag slot? a1+1 dword = offset 4). a1+4 buffer = 64 bytes (since n≤63 + NUL at offset n+4 ≤ 67). Safe bound.\n- If *a1==0 (first tag): malloc(n+73); strcpy(v4+8, \"rootElement\"); memcpy(v4+72, a2, n) — copy n bytes at +72 (v4+72..+72+n), NUL at +72+n ≤ 72+63=135 within malloc(n+73) (n+63 → 136) ✓ safe (1 byte margin: malloc(n+73) so last byte at n+72 alloc'd; NUL at n+72 fine).\n\nsub_41C778 (text cb):\n- n = min(a3, 1975); malloc(n+73); strncpy(v4+8, a1+4, 0x40) (current tag, 64B); memcpy(v4+72, a2, n); NUL at 72+n ≤ 2047 within n+73 (2048) ✓. malloc(n+73) gives bytes 0..n+72; NUL at n+72 OK.\n\nBoth callbacks are bounded (tag 63, text 1975). The SAX parser feeds a3 = v10/v11/v12 lengths from the XML scanning (bounded by < end). So no overflow — the XML value/text path is bounded (1975-byte text cap).\n\nCONCLUSION: minidlna XML/SOAP parse is fully bounded (tag≤63, text≤1975, entity malloc-per-value). Priority-1 item (minidlna SOAP/objectID) closed with clean evidence.\n\nRemaining priorities: vsftpd 虚拟用户与命令解析 — the USER/PASS handlers unnamed. Let me try ONE thing for vsftpd: search pattern \"getPasswdInfo\" callers — in_degree 1; can't name. Search vsftpd for \"auth\" funcs: we saw handle_auth stub. In this TP-Link vsftpd the USER/PASS processing could be in the \"two_process\" — search \"vsf_\" funcs with \"user\": pattern \"user\" limited in vsftpd? Broad. Try pattern \"isUser\"? Search \"passwd_convert\"? Skip — vsftpd input path (ftp_getline+secbuf) already vetted; auth is table-based bounded.\n\nuclited 未扫处理函数 — mostly done. \n\nLet me do a dynamic step for a CURRENT hypothesis per orchestrator: minidlna XML parser — function-level fuzz on ParseNameValue (0x41c8f8) previously handshake-failed. Whole-binary fuzz done. New idea: fuzz **sub_41D224's callback consumer**? Not reachable. Everything has been fuzzed.\n\nOne more NEW static candidate in \"uclited 未扫函数\": **ExecuteVsTable/ExecutePtTable read** (Done), **ucStaticRouteCfg...** (Done), **sendMsgToHwNat** (ipc to kernel module — not code). What about **swReboot** in uclited main — reboot via system? Read it quickly? It's a \"sw_*\" → likely ucReboot → system(\"reboot\") const. Skip.\n\nActually let me close one more real vein: **httpd 的 ucSetDynDnsState/ucSetFirewallDosCfg** etc — config-copy funcs, clean.\n\nGiven priorities exhausted with clean verdicts + 1 new finding this round-chain (PPPoE), the best close: report the ParseNameValue-bound evidence (priority 1 closed), note remaining vsftpd无名 handler issue, and keep state. No new dropbear trace (per instruction). No running fuzz.","stream":true,"block":0}

