data: {"seq":1098,"ts":"2026-08-22T20:44:47.954Z","text":"Only WlanBand wizard init named; the WzdPPPoERpm handler unnamed. The wizard pre-auth question can't be resolved further statically without symbols.\n\nI'm hitting diminishing returns on static names. Let me do a genuinely USEFUL dynamic step the orchestrator allows (配额还在): whole-binary fuzz on a target not yet fuzzed with a hypothesis — none left on inputs... BUT what about fuzzing **httpd with args**? whole-binary ignores argv; but function-level on a STARTUP-reachable httpd function: sub_425CB8? startup reach? No.\n\nAlternatively, use remaining fuzz on **minidlna with argv via whole-binary mode**? argv not supported.\n\nOK — the honest actionable item per orchestrator: \"继续静态深挖并入库\"。I have one more STRONG static candidate I started but never fully verified: **httpd nasFtpSetUserList sprintf(v3[...] or s[256], \"/tmp/vsftp/root/%s\", user)** — the sprintf overflow needs user>238. What's the FTP username max on web? Unknown; but there's a related unchecked copy I DID NOT verify: in **httpd nasSetSrvUserList → nasFtpSetUserList** — the FTP filename builder... same family.\n\nActually here's a better one — I noticed earlier in sub_49D184 (NasFolderSharingRpm): `strncpy((char *)&s[64], v7, 0x10u)` admin name 16B; `strncpy((char *)&s[68], v8, 0x10u)` admin pwd 16B (bounded). BUT in the accountSave path: these then go via swNasSetSrvUserList → nasSetSrvUserList → nasSambaSetUserList (httpd 0x5471d0) — in nasSambaSetUserList the smbpasswd args are `a1[44*idx+2]`(user) and `a1[44*idx+6]`(pwd) — for idx=0 (admin), that's offsets 8/24 of the a1+72 struct — DIFFERENT from s[64]/s[68] (offset 256/272)! So the admin-entry smbpasswd comes from the same user-list entries (which are filled by OTHER buttons in the page, e.g., adding NAS accounts with full username/pwd rows). Fine — regardless, entries are user-controlled strings; the injection stands.\n\nFor a NEW recordable item, let me check the one httpd fragment with a