data: {"seq":25,"ts":"2026-08-22T21:05:46.133Z","text":"Trace quota raised to 48! Do protocol injection now:\n1. **dhcp6s:547 UDP payload** — DHCPv6 Solicit packet → dhcp6_get_options parser coverage! Construct a DHCPv6 Solicit with client-id (DUID) + IA_NA etc. dhcp6s argv needs interface (eth0…) — earlier dhcp6s trace failed because ifinit(\"eth0\") fails under qemu. dhcp6s argv [\"-f\",\"-c\",\"/tmp/x\",\"eth0\"]? eth0 nonexistent → ifinit fail → exit. Hmm — but maybe with -f non-daemon and iface \"lo\"? ifinit(\"lo\") — qemu has lo? if_nametoindex(\"lo\") inside qemu-user maps to host? Under qemu-user getifaddrs/if_nametoindex may work via host netns (docker has lo). Try argv [\"-f\",\"-c\",\"/tmp/dhcp6s.conf\",\"lo\"] with config file content (via input? no - input only for qemu_exec... trace has no input_path). dhcp6s -c needs config file in sandbox rootfs — not writable via trace. But dhcp6s can run without -c? cfparse(NULL) → default /etc/dhcp6s.conf missing → parse fail → exit? main: cfparse(off_43C078[0]) — off_43C078[0]=NULL → maybe uses default conf; error path.\n\nJust try: argv [\"-f\",\"lo\"] port 547 payload_hex DHCPv6 Solicit. Even if it exits early, the trace records. Payload: DHCPv6 Solicit:\n- 1 byte msg-type=1 (Solicit) + 3B txid + options: Client Identifier (opt 1) len, DUID; Elapsed time (opt 8) len2; Option Request (opt 6).\nConstruct hex:\n01 123456 (msg+txid)\nopt1 (ClientID): 0001 000a 0003 0001 001122334455 (DUID-LL: type3 hwtype1 mac6 = 10B)\nopt8 (elapsed): 0008 0002 000a\nopt6 (ORO): 0006 0004 0017 0018 (request DNS 23, NTP 31? 0x17=23 dns, 0x18=24? whatever)\ntotal payload.\n\nhex:\n01123456\n0001 000a 00 03 0001 001122334455\n0008 0002 000a\n0006 0004 0017 0018\n= \"01123456\" + \"0001\" \"000a\" \"00030001001122334455\" + \"00080002\" \"000a\" + \"00060004\" \"0017\" \"0018\"\nconcat: 011234560001000a0003000100112233445500080002000a0006000400170018\n\n2. **smbd SMB1 negprot payload_hex** — send proper SMB negprot (raw SMB over TCP):